1
00:00:00,060 --> 00:00:03,120
How close will Gliese 710 come

2
00:00:03,220 --> 00:00:03,840
to the Sun?

3
00:00:04,120 --> 00:00:05,550
The star will not come anywhere

4
00:00:05,590 --> 00:00:06,660
near the planets.

5
00:00:06,820 --> 00:00:08,150
Make the gap between the sun

6
00:00:08,170 --> 00:00:09,900
and Earth one centimeter.

7
00:00:10,060 --> 00:00:11,920
Neptune, our outermost planet,

8
00:00:12,080 --> 00:00:14,180
is then 30 centimeters away.

9
00:00:14,340 --> 00:00:17,040
And Gliese 710 passes more than

10
00:00:17,140 --> 00:00:18,400
100 meters away,

11
00:00:18,560 --> 00:00:20,120
the length of a football pitch.

12
00:00:20,300 --> 00:00:21,380
That is about a fifth of

13
00:00:21,420 --> 00:00:22,100
a light-year.
